  "body": "Hi,\n\ncould anybody explain what is coming here\n\noriginal markup\n\n``` html\n<!doctype html>\n...\n<body>\n...\n  <svg>\n    <text>\n      some text content\n      <unknown-tag>\n        some contents of unknown tag\n        <span>some spanned contents **belonging to unknown-tag**</span>\n      </unknown-tag>\n    </text>\n  </svg>\n</body></html>\n```\n\nand after parsing we get the following:\n\n``` html\n...\n  <svg>\n    <text>\n      some text content\n      <unknown-tag>\n        some contents of unknown tag  \n      </unknown-tag>\n    </text>\n  </svg>\n  <span>some spanned contents **belonging to unknown-tag**</span>\n...\n```\n\nas per [HTML Standard](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/syntax.html#parsing-main-inforeign), the quote\n\n> 12.2.5.5 The rules for parsing tokens in foreign content\n> \n> When the user agent is to apply the rules for parsing tokens in foreign content, the user agent must handle the token as follows:\n> ...\n> A start tag whose tag name is one of: [long list, including `<span />`]\n> Parse Error\n\nNext, there are an actions defined for this situation\n\n> If the parser was originally created for the HTML fragment parsing algorithm, then act as described in the \"any other start tag\" entry below. \n> \n> Otherwise:\n> \n> Pop an element from the stack of open elements, and then keep popping more elements from the stack of open elements until the current node is a MathML text integration point, an HTML integration point, or an element in the HTML namespace\n\nAnd currently, the behaviour is as per 'otherwise'.\n\nSo questions. Are not browsers' **parsers were originally created for the HTML fragment parsing algorithm**?\n\nif not then why rules of HTML standard applied?\n\nThere is a [demo](http://codepen.io/djFD/full/QKbvGa/), tested in firefox and chromium\n\n**UPD** `\"any other start tag\"`'s algorithm can be clearly seen in this example: `<unknown-tag />` was leaved untouched, as is, and assigned to be a part of SVG namespace ([full algorithm](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/syntax.html#parsing-main-inforeign))\n",
